<title>DENMARK: FORECAST - Citibank ups Danish 1996 GDP, c/a surplus.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Citibank ups Danish 1996 GDP, c/a surplus.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>In its latest survey U.S. Citibank on Thursday raised its expectations for Denmark's 1996 GDP (gross domestic product) growth to 2.1 percent from 1.3 percent in its last forecast in November.</p>
<p>At the same time it upped its 1996 forecast for the current account surplus to 14.0 billion crowns from 7.5 billion crowns, leaving its estimate for inflation unchanged at 2.2 percent.</p>
<p>The latest Danish Econony Ministry forecast in October foresaw 2.0 percent GDP growth, 2.1 percent inflation, 8.9 percent unemployment and a current account surplus of 10.3 billion crowns for this year.</p>
<p>The following estimates were made by 10 leading local and international organisations.</p>
<p>	  (pct)	 GDP    inflation  unemployment c/a (bln Dkk)</p>
<p>Citibank (12/96)    2.1    2.2	  9.0	   14.0</p>
<p>PaineWebber (12/96) 1.8    2.2	  8.4	    8.1</p>
<p>Goldman Sachs(11/96)2.4    2.1	  9.0	   10.5</p>
<p>Conf Dan Ind (11/96)2.2    2.1	  --	    12.0</p>
<p>NatWest(11/96)	1.9    2.3	  9.0	    6.9</p>
<p>Unidanmark (11/96)  2.0    2.1	  9.0	   11.0</p>
<p>Citibank (11/96)    1.3    2.2	  8.3	    7.5</p>
<p>Chase (11/96)	 1.8    2.1	  --	     9.0</p>
<p>Svenska HB (11/96)  2.0    2.1	  8.8	   10.0</p>
<p>M Grenfell (11/96)  1.8    2.1	  8.7	   12.0</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
</text>
